From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Qoder <qoder@localhost>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:15:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] devicemonitor: Post DEVICE_MONITOR_STARTED before signalling
 completion

monitor_thread_func() cleared priv->start_thread and broadcast the
completion condition before posting DEVICE_MONITOR_STARTED on the bus.
gst_device_monitor_stop() steals start_thread to join it, so once the
thread had cleared that pointer it could no longer be joined. It was
then possible for stop() to return, the monitor to be restarted (which
unflushes the bus), and only afterwards for the stale STARTED message
to be posted - landing ahead of the new session's DEVICE_ADDED messages.

Reproduced on upstream main (d4c1c002) by running the gst_gstdevice test
on a single CPU: test_device_monitor got DEVICE_MONITOR_STARTED (0x80000009)
instead of DEVICE_ADDED on its first pop.

Post the message while the thread is still joinable, i.e. before clearing
start_thread, and keep the old placement for the cancelled path.
diff --git a/subprojects/gstreamer/gst/gstdevicemonitor.c b/subprojects/gstreamer/gst/gstdevicemonitor.c
index 2c44936..a1c62ec 100644
--- a/subprojects/gstreamer/gst/gstdevicemonitor.c
+++ b/subprojects/gstreamer/gst/gstdevicemonitor.c
@@ -505,6 +505,7 @@ static gpointer
 monitor_thread_func (gpointer data)
 {
   GSList *started = NULL;
+  gboolean posted = FALSE;
   GQueue pending = G_QUEUE_INIT;
   GstDeviceMonitor *monitor = data;
   GstDeviceProvider *provider;
@@ -567,14 +568,28 @@ monitor_thread_func (gpointer data)
     monitor->priv->started = FALSE;
   }
 
+  /* Post the started message before signalling completion below: otherwise
+   * gst_device_monitor_stop() can miss the thread (start_thread is cleared
+   * before the message is posted) and return to the caller, while this thread
+   * still posts a stale DEVICE_MONITOR_STARTED that ends up on the bus of a
+   * subsequent restart. */
+  GST_OBJECT_UNLOCK (monitor);
+  gst_bus_post (monitor->priv->bus,
+      gst_message_new_device_monitor_started (GST_OBJECT (monitor),
+          started != NULL));
+  GST_OBJECT_LOCK (monitor);
+  posted = TRUE;
+
   g_clear_pointer (&monitor->priv->start_thread, g_thread_unref);
   g_cond_broadcast (&monitor->priv->started_cond);
   GST_OBJECT_UNLOCK (monitor);
 
 done:
-  gst_bus_post (monitor->priv->bus,
-      gst_message_new_device_monitor_started (GST_OBJECT (monitor),
-          started != NULL));
+  if (!posted) {
+    gst_bus_post (monitor->priv->bus,
+        gst_message_new_device_monitor_started (GST_OBJECT (monitor),
+            started != NULL));
+  }
   gst_object_unref (monitor);
 
   return NULL;
